The Add sheet's "Removed from magpie" row of Codex signs the
subscription out for good, and its ask says Codex itself is signed out
too, as codex logout does. forgetLogins kept that promise only for the
sign-ins magpie had saved: Logins(agent) is logins.json, so the sign-in
Codex itself holds went untouched when none of the saved copies named
it — removed from magpie before any look saved it (a saving waits for
its look, due once in 30 seconds, and once removed magpie saves nothing
of the agent), or Codex signed in to another account itself after the
removal. The forget said done, and the row stood there all the same,
still signed in, with a Sign out… that said done and changed nothing,
every time (#5916).

The sign-in the agent holds, which no saved copy named, is signed out
too now — through the same ForgetLogin that signs the saved flow's last
account out, deleteCodexLogin and all (#2367). Claude Code is never
signed out (claudeStandIn), and the other agents' own sign-ins the ask
leaves as they are, so the branch is Codex's alone.

Run:
- TestForgetAccountSignsOutASignInNoSavedCopyNamed: Codex signed in,
  removed before any look saved it, the row's Sign out… — red before
  (the row still listed, auth.json kept), green after (row gone,
  auth.json gone, nothing saved).
- TestForgetAccountSignsOutTheSignInItMovedOnTo: removed, then Codex
  signed in to another account itself — red before, green after.
- Ablation: the branch taken out made both red again (the flow magpie
  saved, TestForgetAccountSignsCodexOut, green either way); restored,
  green.
- ./internal/provider whole green; the four sign-out tests green with
  -race; the whole tree builds with -tags nogui.
- Sibling scan: forgetLogins has the one caller, ForgetAccount;
  deleteCodexLogin the one caller it had; every liveLogin("codex")
  reader reads fresh and reads none once the forget is done
  (autoreset, access-only, resets, switch, import, export); the
  excluded row's readers — the Providers page's reminder line, the Add
  sheet's removed section, magpie accounts / magpie providers — all
  heal from the one data face; savedButSignedOut and the claude and
  plugin paths untouched.

